From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:23:53 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sm8250: create the headset jack on every card
 bind

jack_setup stays true after the card is unbound and snd_card_free() has
freed the headset jack. The next bind then skips the jack creation: the
card comes back without jack controls or a jack input device, and the
MBHC reports into the freed jack.

Clear jack_setup in the link exit for the same links whose init sets up
the headset jack. The exit runs for every initialised link on unbind and
on a failed bind, so the next bind creates the jack again.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
index e9dbbee4a..601e0f85c 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
@@ -49,10 +49,17 @@ static void sm8250_snd_exit(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd)
 	struct sm8250_snd_data *data = snd_soc_card_get_drvdata(rtd->card);
 	struct snd_soc_dai *cpu_dai = snd_soc_rtd_to_cpu(rtd, 0);
 
-	if (cpu_dai->id == USB_RX)
+	switch (cpu_dai->id) {
+	case DISPLAY_PORT_RX:
+		break;
+	case USB_RX:
 		qcom_snd_usb_offload_jack_remove(rtd,
 						 &data->usb_offload_jack_setup);
-
+		break;
+	default:
+		data->jack_setup = false;
+		break;
+	}
 }
 
 static int sm8250_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
